WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:05.209
Six months since the Taliban seized power
and the killing and other human rights abuses

00:00:05.209 --> 00:00:07.660
have gone on multiplying.

00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:12.880
Women have been a major target – their peaceful
protests broken up, some have been threatened,

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:14.830
beaten and disappeared.

00:00:14.830 --> 00:00:17.230
The Taliban had promised an inclusive government.

00:00:17.230 --> 00:00:20.710
But not a single woman was appointed to the
cabinet.

00:00:20.710 --> 00:00:25.980
My guest this week from Kabul is Shafiullah
Azam, Taliban director general of economic

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:28.140
relations at the foreign ministry.

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:33.960
“Are you and the Taliban capable of anything
more constructive than violence and repression?”

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:39.879
“We are working on our police forces, before
they were warriors for 20 years but after

00:00:39.879 --> 00:00:44.489
that they changed the role from warriors to
policemen.”

00:00:44.489 --> 00:00:46.859
But what future are they building?

00:00:46.859 --> 00:00:52.449
Sources tell DW that the drug trade is booming
and the Taliban is still taking its cut, as

00:00:52.449 --> 00:00:54.649
it has done for years.

00:00:54.649 --> 00:00:59.190
And will they crackdown on some of the world’s
most dangerous terror groups, openly hosted

00:00:59.190 --> 00:01:00.190
in the country.

00:01:00.190 --> 00:01:05.720
Do they really believe they can play nice
with Al Qaida and the West at the same time?

00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:10.670
That and much more on Conflict Zone.

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:18.789
Shafiullah Azam welcome to Conflict Zone.

00:01:18.789 --> 00:01:20.170
Nice to be with you.

00:01:20.170 --> 00:01:25.680
The Taliban made a lot of promises when it
seized power last August, and they've broken

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:26.939
a lot of them.

00:01:26.939 --> 00:01:31.490
Is there any reason why the world should trust
anything they say these days?

00:01:31.490 --> 00:01:39.579
We know a Taliban made or Islamic Emirate
made many promises, but based on their five

00:01:39.579 --> 00:01:48.720
or six months' experience, if we see the changes,
actually it's totally dramatic to not only

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:56.039
to foreigners but as well to Afghans, and
for 20 years, many propaganda has been made

00:01:56.039 --> 00:01:58.390
against Islamic Emirate.

00:01:58.390 --> 00:02:04.829
But while they come to the power and they
clearly show that to everyone, that these

00:02:04.829 --> 00:02:07.720
were rumors, fake news and propaganda.

00:02:07.720 --> 00:02:12.970
Alright Mr. Azam, let me just, pick you up
on that, because you said they have been,

00:02:12.970 --> 00:02:17.100
rightly, in power for almost a year, almost
half a year.

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:23.210
The UN and other human rights bodies continue
to release deeply disturbing reports of their

00:02:23.210 --> 00:02:25.050
human rights violations.

00:02:25.050 --> 00:02:27.010
Aren't you ashamed of that?

00:02:27.010 --> 00:02:35.000
Before this report, a representative of UN
had a meeting with the interior minister,

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:43.000
and they said they showed their satisfaction
from security and to all members of the UN

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:44.000
as well.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:51.450
On 6 February, we had a meeting with UN, all
organizations, which are UNAMA, and they showed

00:02:51.450 --> 00:02:58.060
their satisfaction from the current new government
that they provided well security to all of

00:02:58.060 --> 00:03:00.890
UN members, then that they have access to...

00:03:00.890 --> 00:03:05.890
Apart from UN members, your officials claimed
repeatedly there were amnesties for those

00:03:05.890 --> 00:03:07.980
who worked for the previous government.

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:13.870
And yet the UN has revealed credible evidence
that your fighters have gone on hunting down

00:03:13.870 --> 00:03:16.750
and killing those who've already surrendered.

00:03:16.750 --> 00:03:21.330
The UN said just two months ago that between
August and November last year, they received

00:03:21.330 --> 00:03:27.480
evidence of more than 100 killings of former
Afghan security personnel and others associated

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:28.480
with the government.

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:31.900
72 of those killings attributed to the Taliban.

00:03:31.900 --> 00:03:37.760
In several cases, the bodies of those victims
were publicly displayed.

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:45.290
How do you justify those crimes attributed
directly to the Taliban?

00:03:45.290 --> 00:03:52.750
One thing should be considered: that since
six month, or at least if we want to compare

00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:57.940
the situation, there should be some indicators
to compare that with the previous.

00:03:57.940 --> 00:04:05.820
In a previous regime, each single day, we
were losing around 300 Afghans in both sides.

00:04:05.820 --> 00:04:07.190
That's not a fair comparison.

00:04:07.190 --> 00:04:11.580
I'm talking about what you've done since you
came to power.

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:12.610
I'm coming to that.

00:04:12.610 --> 00:04:14.320
I'm coming to that.

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:20.220
Based on policy level, there is a clear amnesty
to everyone.

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:27.180
Yes, we can accept it that now we are not
carrying heritage of 20 years' war.

00:04:27.180 --> 00:04:31.740
But now, right now, we are carrying heritage
of 43-year war.

00:04:31.740 --> 00:04:38.840
Yes, in some cases there would be some incidents
of violation, but it doesn't mean it's a policy

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:40.590
of the government.

00:04:40.590 --> 00:04:44.740
Government is following those cases and everyone
would be brought to justice.

00:04:44.740 --> 00:04:46.620
So your fighters are out of control.

00:04:46.620 --> 00:04:47.910
Is this what you're telling me?

00:04:47.910 --> 00:04:49.630
Your fighters are out of control?

00:04:49.630 --> 00:04:51.790
No, no, no, no.

00:04:51.790 --> 00:04:52.790
I can clearly see that our fighters...

00:04:52.790 --> 00:04:56.190
... well either you order these killings or
the fighters are out of control, which is

00:04:56.190 --> 00:04:57.940
it?

00:04:57.940 --> 00:05:00.150
Our fighters are under control.

00:05:00.150 --> 00:05:05.630
If they were not, we would be witness of hundreds
of killings in Afghanistan.

00:05:05.630 --> 00:05:09.760
You know better, in 20 years, many wrong things
happen to everyone.

00:05:09.760 --> 00:05:14.690
There would be many private cases between
different parties.

00:05:14.690 --> 00:05:21.410
But this is, it shows commitment of the government
and for the rest of these violations government

00:05:21.410 --> 00:05:24.540
have a full commitment and they will bring
them to justice.

00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:25.540
How do we know that?

00:05:25.540 --> 00:05:26.540
How do we know that?

00:05:26.540 --> 00:05:27.540
How do we know?

00:05:27.540 --> 00:05:29.260
We only have your word for that?

00:05:29.260 --> 00:05:31.560
As far as your justice is concerned, we have
no idea.

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:35.270
There's no independent monitoring of that.

00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:37.340
So we only have your word for this.

00:05:37.340 --> 00:05:38.700
No, no.

00:05:38.700 --> 00:05:43.720
One thing is that the international community
expectation is totally high.

00:05:43.720 --> 00:05:46.440
They are not considering the current situation.

00:05:46.440 --> 00:05:52.380
We are not living in a Western country that
was calm for hundreds of years.

00:05:52.380 --> 00:05:58.780
Still, we move from a conflict zone to to
this, to the peace, to the

00:05:58.780 --> 00:05:59.780
stability.

00:05:59.780 --> 00:06:04.300
Yes, there would be some stability, but this
is a positive point that government have a

00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:06.280
full commitment for that.

00:06:06.280 --> 00:06:09.430
And still they have control many cases...

00:06:09.430 --> 00:06:14.190
Mr. Azam, you are only being measured, you're
only being measured by the promises that you've

00:06:14.190 --> 00:06:18.670
made, not by any other standards and you've
broken a lot of those promises.

00:06:18.670 --> 00:06:25.470
As recently as last month, the United Nations
reported credible allegations of illegal disappearances

00:06:25.470 --> 00:06:30.770
and said a growing number of the Taliban's
political opponents are being detained, along

00:06:30.770 --> 00:06:34.850
with civil society representatives and people
who voice dissent.

00:06:34.850 --> 00:06:38.710
Children are also being detained indefinitely.

00:06:38.710 --> 00:06:39.790
You think that's fair?

00:06:39.790 --> 00:06:41.780
You think that's just?

00:06:41.780 --> 00:06:49.090
Right now, if you see, if you compare the
propaganda going against Islamic Emirate,

00:06:49.090 --> 00:06:52.090
now we have free press everywhere.

00:06:52.090 --> 00:06:53.960
Everyone has their own voices.

00:06:53.960 --> 00:06:59.020
Yes, in some cases there would be some investigation
regarding something.

00:06:59.020 --> 00:07:04.550
One thing is clear: in every government and
every country, there is a rule for freedom

00:07:04.550 --> 00:07:06.860
of speech, for protest, for everything.

00:07:06.860 --> 00:07:10.620
Everyone have a right to raise their voice
and protest.

00:07:10.620 --> 00:07:17.480
But they should not disrespect values of the
whole country, and they should not do an action

00:07:17.480 --> 00:07:20.840
to lead a country to destabilization.

00:07:20.840 --> 00:07:23.870
Stability for current government is a priority.

00:07:23.870 --> 00:07:32.110
We are going toward stability to bring security
in our country and to the region and to international

00:07:32.110 --> 00:07:33.110
community.

00:07:33.110 --> 00:07:40.840
Yes, in some cases, in some cases, the government
has a right to investigate from everyone.

00:07:40.840 --> 00:07:42.190
To bring everyone to the justice.

00:07:42.190 --> 00:07:43.410
This is a right.

00:07:43.410 --> 00:07:50.090
But one thing is clear in policy level: that
Afghan current government is completely committed

00:07:50.090 --> 00:07:51.750
to the freedom of press.

00:07:51.750 --> 00:07:54.420
As they mentioned recently.

00:07:54.420 --> 00:08:00.449
They declared in a statement, just requested
from the media and for all users of that,

00:08:00.449 --> 00:08:01.449
they should consider.

00:08:01.449 --> 00:08:04.290
Mr. Azam, you talk about, you talk about the
freedom of the press.

00:08:04.290 --> 00:08:08.410
Since August, more than 6,000 journalists
have lost their jobs.

00:08:08.410 --> 00:08:11.930
80% of female journalists are no longer working.

00:08:11.930 --> 00:08:15.960
You've closed more than 40% of the media outlets
in the country.

00:08:15.960 --> 00:08:19.660
Instead of press freedom, this looks as though
you're scared of the truth.

00:08:19.660 --> 00:08:23.640
What makes you and the Taliban so scared of
the truth?

00:08:23.640 --> 00:08:29.419
Mr. Sebastian, you are a person that you are
completely aware from Afghan current situation.

00:08:29.419 --> 00:08:34.529
These journalists, which they have lost their
job, this is not because the policy level

00:08:34.529 --> 00:08:35.569
or the policy of Afghan government.

00:08:35.569 --> 00:08:36.899
Let’s look at the policy.

00:08:36.899 --> 00:08:37.940
Let's look at the policy.

00:08:37.940 --> 00:08:40.539
We have your new journalism code.

00:08:40.539 --> 00:08:46.440
Media outlets are told they must prepare,
quote, "detailed reports in coordination with

00:08:46.440 --> 00:08:49.249
the government media and information center."

00:08:49.249 --> 00:08:50.249
Why?

00:08:50.249 --> 00:08:51.470
So you can censor the stories.

00:08:51.470 --> 00:08:53.660
Is that the aim?

00:08:53.660 --> 00:08:58.490
This coordination doesn't mean that they should
hide the realities.

00:08:58.490 --> 00:09:04.550
This coordination mean that everything should
be based on rules and regulation, based on

00:09:04.550 --> 00:09:06.139
the rules of journalism.

00:09:06.139 --> 00:09:12.240
In some cases, in some cases we have seen
that many are making propaganda because of

00:09:12.240 --> 00:09:14.990
their personal interests to get asylum.

00:09:14.990 --> 00:09:22.070
Just control on these issues is important
for the government and from everywhere.

00:09:22.070 --> 00:09:24.850
Right now, we are requesting from media and
many

00:09:24.850 --> 00:09:30.709
other activities just they should reflect
what is really going on on the ground, not

00:09:30.709 --> 00:09:32.100
what they are imagining.

00:09:32.100 --> 00:09:38.189
So show respect, you show respect, do you,
for freedom of the press and for journalists?

00:09:38.189 --> 00:09:43.769
This wasn't on show last September, when journalists
covering demonstrations were rounded up, and

00:09:43.769 --> 00:09:50.079
photos later showed the backs of two reporters
covered with bruises and gashes from being

00:09:50.079 --> 00:09:53.259
whipped with cables by your thugs.

00:09:53.259 --> 00:09:56.779
Does that sound respectful to you?

00:09:56.779 --> 00:09:57.850
One thing should be clear.

00:09:57.850 --> 00:09:58.850
Listen to me.

00:09:58.850 --> 00:10:04.730
Why you are totally differentiat[ing] Afghan
government from the other side of the other

00:10:04.730 --> 00:10:06.680
countries?

00:10:06.680 --> 00:10:11.429
The same incident, same thing can happen in
Western countries as well.

00:10:11.429 --> 00:10:17.540
We have many videos that show how police of
western European countries, the US, they are

00:10:17.540 --> 00:10:18.579
treating women.

00:10:18.579 --> 00:10:20.043
Their behavior is so brutal against them.

00:10:20.043 --> 00:10:23.350
Mr. Azam, we are not talking about other countries,
we are talking about Afghanistan...

00:10:23.350 --> 00:10:24.550
... the problem, the problem...

00:10:24.550 --> 00:10:27.339
You can play the "what about” game indefinitely.

00:10:27.339 --> 00:10:28.929
"What about" other places?

00:10:28.929 --> 00:10:30.639
I'm talking to you about Afghanistan.

00:10:30.639 --> 00:10:32.019
That's it.

00:10:32.019 --> 00:10:41.249
If any behavior is not suitable to be done
with the protesters or many other activists,

00:10:41.249 --> 00:10:45.120
it doesn't mean that we are happy, government
is happy on that.

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:49.899
Yes, but in a ground, something can happen
and it's common everywhere.

00:10:49.899 --> 00:10:57.629
But the problem is, why some TV channels some
groups of countries they are, they made Afghanistan

00:10:57.629 --> 00:10:58.629
under watch.

00:10:58.629 --> 00:11:03.089
They are broadcasting very small issues in
a very wide manner.

00:11:03.089 --> 00:11:04.170
This is a problem.

00:11:04.170 --> 00:11:07.810
Let's come to the reality, to the neutrality.

00:11:07.810 --> 00:11:13.199
Consider current situation of every country
[and] based on that, make calculation against

00:11:13.199 --> 00:11:14.199
them.

00:11:14.199 --> 00:11:19.889
We're talking about your country and the concerns
being expressed at what is going on in your

00:11:19.889 --> 00:11:21.899
country from the highest level.

00:11:21.899 --> 00:11:26.430
The U.N. secretary-general said last month
he remained extremely concerned about the

00:11:26.430 --> 00:11:31.209
fate of several women activists who have been
abducted from their homes and have disappeared.

00:11:31.209 --> 00:11:36.121
No Afghan, he said, should live in fear of
a knock at their door in the night, and no

00:11:36.121 --> 00:11:41.220
family should be left to wonder about the
whereabouts and fate of their loved ones.

00:11:41.220 --> 00:11:43.309
But they are living in fear, aren't they?

00:11:43.309 --> 00:11:49.139
And creating that fear seems to have been
your primary achievement over the last half-year.

00:11:49.139 --> 00:11:54.989
Are you in the Taliban capable of anything
more constructive than violence and repression?

00:11:54.989 --> 00:11:59.949
Because we've seen a lot of that from you?

00:11:59.949 --> 00:12:05.410
My point is this that every comment or claims,
which is made on current government, just

00:12:05.410 --> 00:12:11.730
compare that to the previous government which
used … and they were glorifying that we

00:12:11.730 --> 00:12:15.839
are making good governance here.

00:12:15.839 --> 00:12:16.839
Compared to that...

00:12:16.839 --> 00:12:20.960
I know you want to talk about the other government,
but we're talking about your government.

00:12:20.960 --> 00:12:21.960
...these types of incidents was happening
on that time as well.

00:12:21.960 --> 00:12:22.960
: We're talking about your government.

00:12:22.960 --> 00:12:23.960
… at that time as well.

00:12:23.960 --> 00:12:24.960
Right now, right now...

00:12:24.960 --> 00:12:25.960
I know you want to change the subject...

00:12:25.960 --> 00:12:26.960
I do not.

00:12:26.960 --> 00:12:29.649
I not reject that that there would be no mistake.

00:12:29.649 --> 00:12:30.649
Sure.

00:12:30.649 --> 00:12:32.589
Everything can happen everywhere.

00:12:32.589 --> 00:12:37.279
But based on policy level, it's not the policy.

00:12:37.279 --> 00:12:43.110
The current government within five months,
they control many many better compared to

00:12:43.110 --> 00:12:44.550
the previous regime.

00:12:44.550 --> 00:12:45.889
This is achievement.

00:12:45.889 --> 00:12:48.920
No one is exposing this type of achievement.

00:12:48.920 --> 00:12:50.689
Just they are making criticize.

00:12:50.689 --> 00:12:53.750
In some thing there would be some violations.

00:12:53.750 --> 00:12:58.360
We accept that there is some personal cases,
some personal behavior.

00:12:58.360 --> 00:13:03.740
Right now, we are working on our police forces
— before they were warriors for 20 years.

00:13:03.740 --> 00:13:08.819
But after that they changed the role of warrior
to the policemen.

00:13:08.819 --> 00:13:14.319
Right now, every single day, if you ask from
Kabul citizen or many other citizens all over

00:13:14.319 --> 00:13:18.079
the country, there is a positive movement.

00:13:18.079 --> 00:13:21.050
We have many progress in this situation.

00:13:21.050 --> 00:13:26.550
They provided well security to every Afghan,
to foreigners, which they are here.

00:13:26.550 --> 00:13:31.139
It's unacceptable to everyone compared to
the propaganda.

00:13:31.139 --> 00:13:35.580
And a lot of concern being expressed at high
level, Mr. Azam.

00:13:35.580 --> 00:13:38.800
The UN sees a pattern in the Taliban's behavior.

00:13:38.800 --> 00:13:44.379
It talks of arbitrary arrests and detentions,
as well as torture and ill treatment of civil

00:13:44.379 --> 00:13:50.249
society activists, journalists and media workers,
along with former government and security

00:13:50.249 --> 00:13:51.920
forces personnel.

00:13:51.920 --> 00:13:56.309
That adds up to a pretty shameful record,
doesn't it?

00:13:56.309 --> 00:14:00.100
This is not in a level that they are expressing
that.

00:14:00.100 --> 00:14:06.160
In some cases, I accept that there would be
some problems, but it doesn't shows the policy

00:14:06.160 --> 00:14:07.160
level.

00:14:07.160 --> 00:14:12.309
In some cases, there are some groups are making
some videos, they are making some propaganda.

00:14:12.309 --> 00:14:14.879
I can give you an example of that.

00:14:14.879 --> 00:14:21.429
Right now, Afghan government didn’t force
no one, no woman to wear a burqa.

00:14:21.429 --> 00:14:26.920
They let them just decide as an advice, that
[you should] adjust yourself based on Islamic

00:14:26.920 --> 00:14:28.300
and Afghan value.

00:14:28.300 --> 00:14:31.740
But in some cases, some are coming [and] they
are burning burqa.

00:14:31.740 --> 00:14:33.139
What does it mean?

00:14:33.139 --> 00:14:36.749
Actually, this is an act of destabilizing.

00:14:36.749 --> 00:14:42.220
They are bringing pressure on police that
to show an action and to make a propaganda

00:14:42.220 --> 00:14:43.220
on that.

00:14:43.220 --> 00:14:44.230
Let me just make this point to you.

00:14:44.230 --> 00:14:47.879
You say nobody is being forced to wear the
hijab or the burqa.

00:14:47.879 --> 00:14:49.249
That's simply not true.

00:14:49.249 --> 00:14:55.360
On February the 7th General Mubeen Khan, spokesman
for your Kabul Police, said "it's not up to

00:14:55.360 --> 00:14:58.329
the people to say we choose the coverings
we like.

00:14:58.329 --> 00:15:00.980
No, you do what we prescribe.

00:15:00.980 --> 00:15:01.990
Period.

00:15:01.990 --> 00:15:03.449
You do what we prescribe."

00:15:03.449 --> 00:15:07.100
And he added, "the Taliban's patience is running
thin."

00:15:07.100 --> 00:15:14.540
So Mr. Azam, they are being forced and told
what to wear, contrary to your comfortable

00:15:14.540 --> 00:15:16.490
assurances.

00:15:16.490 --> 00:15:22.689
If it is right, right now, ask from your reporters,
and they should see Kabul's situation, other

00:15:22.689 --> 00:15:28.519
cities' situation, so why, this is not physical
existence, what you are claiming?

00:15:28.519 --> 00:15:30.850
Actually, this is not a policy.

00:15:30.850 --> 00:15:37.350
Don't make an excuse of one person as a policy
— policy is totally different.

00:15:37.350 --> 00:15:38.699
Right now Afghan government encourages everyone...

00:15:38.699 --> 00:15:42.429
He is the police spokesman for Kabul, he's
the Kabul police spokesman.

00:15:42.429 --> 00:15:43.649
He's not.

00:15:43.649 --> 00:15:45.720
He's a police spokesperson.

00:15:45.720 --> 00:15:51.930
Maybe because of such claims, which is not
representing policy of Afghan government policymakers

00:15:51.930 --> 00:15:53.589
or others.

00:15:53.589 --> 00:15:56.699
And there are others which are implementing
the rules.

00:15:56.699 --> 00:16:05.420
Right now, the situation which is provided
within this …, this is totally unexpected.

00:16:05.420 --> 00:16:13.989
And Afghan government is working to regularize
all activities to bring that type of facilities,

00:16:13.989 --> 00:16:20.759
services to Afghans, which they are in need
of that, that meet their religious and cultural

00:16:20.759 --> 00:16:21.809
values.

00:16:21.809 --> 00:16:24.230
This is a very positive change.

00:16:24.230 --> 00:16:28.910
And the women, and the women, the way women
are being treated, is not a positive change.

00:16:28.910 --> 00:16:34.139
The fact is they've become second class citizens
— pushed around, forced to wear what you

00:16:34.139 --> 00:16:35.139
decide.

00:16:35.139 --> 00:16:36.139
Study where you decide.

00:16:36.139 --> 00:16:38.089
Work where you decide, if at all.

00:16:38.089 --> 00:16:40.459
Can you give an example?

00:16:40.459 --> 00:16:42.610
What gives you what gives you the right?

00:16:42.610 --> 00:16:47.989
I'll give you an example, and I'll give you
what the UN secretary-general said about this

00:16:47.989 --> 00:16:48.989
just last month.

00:16:48.989 --> 00:16:55.019
He said women scientists, lawyers and teachers
are locked out, locked out, wasting skills

00:16:55.019 --> 00:16:57.899
and talents that will benefit the entire country.

00:16:57.899 --> 00:17:03.459
A generation of girls is seeing its hopes
and dreams shattered.

00:17:03.459 --> 00:17:08.720
How does destroying the girls' hopes and dreams
fit into your Islamic code?

00:17:08.720 --> 00:17:10.470
Please answer that.

00:17:10.470 --> 00:17:11.860
This is not correct.

00:17:11.860 --> 00:17:12.860
Right now...

00:17:12.860 --> 00:17:15.640
So the UN secretary-general doesn't know what
he's talking about.

00:17:15.640 --> 00:17:16.640
Is that it?

00:17:16.640 --> 00:17:17.640
Listen to me.

00:17:17.640 --> 00:17:19.250
I'm not talking about him.

00:17:19.250 --> 00:17:21.140
Let's discuss about the fact.

00:17:21.140 --> 00:17:24.689
I am requesting you do not rely only on reports.

00:17:24.689 --> 00:17:29.110
You can see the current reality which is going
on right now.

00:17:29.110 --> 00:17:32.600
University doors are open to the girls.

00:17:32.600 --> 00:17:39.799
Why you, why you are not reflecting this positive
signals right now in Jalalabad, or in those

00:17:39.799 --> 00:17:46.580
areas which have a hot season right now, women
are going there right now.

00:17:46.580 --> 00:17:52.669
Male and, man and woman, they are registering
their names to the concours, which the entrance

00:17:52.669 --> 00:17:54.400
door to the university.

00:17:54.400 --> 00:17:56.120
Right now, they're registering.

00:17:56.120 --> 00:18:01.940
Why you are not discussing about this right
now, we have more than 15,000 women working

00:18:01.940 --> 00:18:03.529
only in health sector.

00:18:03.529 --> 00:18:10.030
Right now women are working in our passport
directorate, in our identity card directorate,

00:18:10.030 --> 00:18:12.500
in Kabul airport or many other areas.

00:18:12.500 --> 00:18:18.000
Yes, there were some projects, some, some
other organizations.

00:18:18.000 --> 00:18:21.630
The only blame cannot refer to the Taliban.

00:18:21.630 --> 00:18:24.890
International donors, they had many economic
projects.

00:18:24.890 --> 00:18:26.559
They had many other projects.

00:18:26.559 --> 00:18:27.559
They cut their donation.

00:18:27.559 --> 00:18:28.559
Therefore, men and women…

00:18:28.559 --> 00:18:32.080
Are women going to be welcomed back to all
the jobs they had before?

00:18:32.080 --> 00:18:37.910
No, there isn't even a women's ministry anymore
because you closed that down.

00:18:37.910 --> 00:18:40.970
In many countries, there is no ministry for
women.

00:18:40.970 --> 00:18:45.620
It doesn't mean that the current government
ignoring them, right now before I gave many

00:18:45.620 --> 00:18:50.289
example in many ministries, in many organization,
they are doing work.

00:18:50.289 --> 00:18:52.880
They are providing services to men and women.

00:18:52.880 --> 00:18:54.980
There is no policy for that.

00:18:54.980 --> 00:19:01.710
Let's talk about the terrible food shortages,
the humanitarian crisis facing your country,

00:19:01.710 --> 00:19:06.059
what has become a daily nightmare for people
trying to feed their families.

00:19:06.059 --> 00:19:10.850
It wasn't until the first week of this month
that your first deputy prime minister called

00:19:10.850 --> 00:19:15.730
on government departments to present plans
for tackling the crisis.

00:19:15.730 --> 00:19:19.860
What have you been doing for the last six
months?

00:19:19.860 --> 00:19:27.769
Regarding humanitarian aid, there was a concern
for many years that takeover by coming Islamic

00:19:27.769 --> 00:19:32.820
Emirate, we will lose values of 20 years'
achievements.

00:19:32.820 --> 00:19:35.779
Right now Afghan government kept that system
active.

00:19:35.779 --> 00:19:40.580
It's [the] international community — they
are ignoring the system, they are destroying.

00:19:40.580 --> 00:19:44.309
They are making a parallel system which is
difficult for them.

00:19:44.309 --> 00:19:49.019
Difficult for them to distribute the humanitarian
assets or many others.

00:19:49.019 --> 00:19:51.080
They are ignoring banking system.

00:19:51.080 --> 00:19:56.600
Mr Azam, let's talk about the enormous illegal
drug trade in Afghanistan that the Taliban

00:19:56.600 --> 00:20:00.900
has warned that this huge criminal enterprise
will have to stop.

00:20:00.900 --> 00:20:05.170
Does that also apply to the Taliban as well,
since they've been cashing in on the drugs

00:20:05.170 --> 00:20:08.320
trade in parts of Afghanistan for a very long
time?

00:20:08.320 --> 00:20:12.850
Are they going to stop trading in illegal
narcotics as well?

00:20:12.850 --> 00:20:15.500
Come to, come to the policy.

00:20:15.500 --> 00:20:22.190
Right now all narcotic business or trade is
going through our … banking system.

00:20:22.190 --> 00:20:28.130
Right now, Afghan government is totally committed
for re-establishing supporting banking system.

00:20:28.130 --> 00:20:29.130
But sanctions happened...

00:20:29.130 --> 00:20:30.220
I'm talking about the drug business.

00:20:30.220 --> 00:20:32.169
I'm talking about the drug business.

00:20:32.169 --> 00:20:38.230
I'm asking whether your own fighters are going
to stop dealing in drugs and taking taxes

00:20:38.230 --> 00:20:39.230
from it.

00:20:39.230 --> 00:20:43.870
Last year, a report to the UN Security Council
said the production and trafficking of drugs

00:20:43.870 --> 00:20:48.510
remained the Taliban's largest single source
of income.

00:20:48.510 --> 00:20:52.390
Again, how does that fit in with your Islamic
principles?

00:20:52.390 --> 00:20:58.289
These reports were available as well about
the previous government as well, but you can

00:20:58.289 --> 00:21:03.300
say the policy of Afghan current government
in their previous period, which they have

00:21:03.300 --> 00:21:06.590
a government, how they brought that this business
to zero.

00:21:06.590 --> 00:21:07.990
You're not answering my question.

00:21:07.990 --> 00:21:10.000
You're not answering my question.

00:21:10.000 --> 00:21:15.310
Right now, I can say the situation would be
many, many better from a government which

00:21:15.310 --> 00:21:19.740
was supported by US, NATO.

00:21:19.740 --> 00:21:21.480
I can clearly guarantee that.

00:21:21.480 --> 00:21:23.309
I can clearly guarantee.

00:21:23.309 --> 00:21:29.519
Right now, Afghan government is working to
provide alternative in agricultural section.

00:21:29.519 --> 00:21:35.140
If international community relieved their
concerns, they should support our agriculture

00:21:35.140 --> 00:21:36.419
section.

00:21:36.419 --> 00:21:38.390
There would be no business.

00:21:38.390 --> 00:21:43.140
There would be no harvesting of narcotics.

00:21:43.140 --> 00:21:44.140
Can we, can we also...

00:21:44.140 --> 00:21:45.140
Policy is clear.

00:21:45.140 --> 00:21:47.490
If international community is real about their
concern, they should support our agricultural

00:21:47.490 --> 00:21:48.490
sector.

00:21:48.490 --> 00:21:53.950
Mr Azam, can we expect the Taliban will also
fail to keep its promise to prevent terrorist

00:21:53.950 --> 00:21:57.279
groups in your country from launching attacks
outside Afghanistan?

00:21:57.279 --> 00:22:00.519
You are still very friendly with al Qaida.

00:22:00.519 --> 00:22:02.990
Your two groups have even intermarried.

00:22:02.990 --> 00:22:03.990
Many of the leaders are

00:22:03.990 --> 00:22:06.539
based in Afghanistan and the border region.

00:22:06.539 --> 00:22:13.360
How exactly do you intend to prevent them
launching attacks?

00:22:13.360 --> 00:22:16.590
Clear example is available.

00:22:16.590 --> 00:22:20.929
Compared to the previous report, always they
were criticizing that more than 20 terrorist

00:22:20.929 --> 00:22:23.070
groups are active in Afghanistan.

00:22:23.070 --> 00:22:28.700
Actually, these groups rise and born under
U.S., NATO forces.

00:22:28.700 --> 00:22:35.570
But regarding Daesh forces, while Islamic
Emirate was at the same time in fighting against

00:22:35.570 --> 00:22:43.190
previous Afghan regime use NATO forces, they
proved that they eliminated Daesh from all

00:22:43.190 --> 00:22:44.480
over the country.

00:22:44.480 --> 00:22:45.970
This was Afghan government.

00:22:45.970 --> 00:22:49.639
This was international community, many reports
of...

00:22:49.639 --> 00:22:51.860
We're talking about Al Qaida.

00:22:51.860 --> 00:23:00.029
I clearly said, based on Doha agreement, Afghan
current government have a full commitment.

00:23:00.029 --> 00:23:03.580
There would be no threat to Afghans.

00:23:03.580 --> 00:23:08.799
They will not allow every single group to
make a threat to other countries.

00:23:08.799 --> 00:23:09.799
This is a full commitment.

00:23:09.799 --> 00:23:13.100
But you allow them to train on your territory.

00:23:13.100 --> 00:23:15.250
You allow them to train on your territory.

00:23:15.250 --> 00:23:20.919
The UN report recently said that under your
rule, these terrorists enjoy greater freedom

00:23:20.919 --> 00:23:25.909
in Afghanistan than at any time in recent
history, and there are no signs you've taken

00:23:25.909 --> 00:23:28.130
steps to limit their activities.

00:23:28.130 --> 00:23:29.130
Why?

00:23:29.130 --> 00:23:30.130
Totally baseless.

00:23:30.130 --> 00:23:31.130
Totally incorrect.

00:23:31.130 --> 00:23:33.520
So they just don't understand what they are
talking about.

00:23:33.520 --> 00:23:34.520
I'm confused.

00:23:34.520 --> 00:23:36.259
I'm confused about these UN reports.

00:23:36.259 --> 00:23:41.230
While their representatives are coming and
they are discussing with our Ministry of Interior,

00:23:41.230 --> 00:23:47.779
Ministry of Defense, they are saying, well
security is provided, well situation in everywhere.

00:23:47.779 --> 00:23:52.649
But on the other side, those reporters, I
don't know who are there from where they are

00:23:52.649 --> 00:23:54.409
receiving this type of reports.

00:23:54.409 --> 00:24:02.570
Clearly, I can say this is the policy of current
government: We want to make a stable country

00:24:02.570 --> 00:24:04.240
instead of conflict zone.

00:24:04.240 --> 00:24:09.929
We are going to the zone of national interest,
to the zone of economic interest.

00:24:09.929 --> 00:24:16.139
We want to reconnect a big project of our
neighbors and regional.

00:24:16.139 --> 00:24:17.210
This is the policy.

00:24:17.210 --> 00:24:22.710
At the same time, with this policy, we cannot
support those groups which are making threats

00:24:22.710 --> 00:24:23.710
to others.

00:24:23.710 --> 00:24:27.159
Yes, there are many heritage from 20 years.

00:24:27.159 --> 00:24:33.629
Afghan government is fighting against them
and we will provide a secure environment for

00:24:33.629 --> 00:24:35.230
all investors.

00:24:35.230 --> 00:24:37.790
You want, you want a secure environment.

00:24:37.790 --> 00:24:42.570
You want a secure environment and a stable
country by hosting some of the most dangerous

00:24:42.570 --> 00:24:44.700
terrorist groups in the world.

00:24:44.700 --> 00:24:49.639
You think the West is going to watch you and
expect you to play nice with those terrorist

00:24:49.639 --> 00:24:51.600
groups and with them at the same time?

00:24:51.600 --> 00:24:54.529
You really think the West is going to accept
that?

00:24:54.529 --> 00:24:56.920
That's totally rejected by Afghan government.

00:24:56.920 --> 00:25:06.330
They called on them to please instead of blaming,
making excuses, provide a proof to the government.

00:25:06.330 --> 00:25:11.530
Based on that, if government didn't take action,
they can claim on that.

00:25:11.530 --> 00:25:18.309
For 20 to 30 years, there was a huge propaganda
against Afghan government.

00:25:18.309 --> 00:25:24.590
Let's, if we want to have a stable country,
and to not be a threat to the neighbor, to

00:25:24.590 --> 00:25:27.809
the region and country, let's support Afghan
government.

00:25:27.809 --> 00:25:29.039
They have a

00:25:29.039 --> 00:25:32.250
good plan for our region, for Afghanistan.

00:25:32.250 --> 00:25:35.500
Main focus is economic development in Afghanistan.

00:25:35.500 --> 00:25:36.500
Let's support.

00:25:36.500 --> 00:25:37.500
Let's give a chance.

00:25:37.500 --> 00:25:38.500
Alright.

00:25:38.500 --> 00:25:41.139
Shafiullah Azam, thanks very much for being
on Conflict Zone.

00:25:41.139 --> 00:25:42.139
Thank you.

00:25:42.139 --> 00:25:43.139
Appreciate your time.

00:25:43.139 --> 00:25:44.139
It's my pleasure.

00:25:44.139 --> 00:25:44.143
Thank you so much.

